body.technical_internal_limitation:
The identity \(\min_{
u\in C}\max_A d_A(
u)=\max_A\min_{
u\in C}d_A(
u)\) is false in general. For \(S=E\setminus\{0\}\), a ternary confidence segment can give values \(7/260\) and \(0\), respectively. The certification program therefore keeps the order \(\min_{
u}\max_A\) or uses the equivalent joint transportation linear program; it never chooses one Hall cut uniformly over the confidence region.
